<td id="A1.T5.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Manifold Muon</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Dual-ascent steps</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">20</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T5.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Manifold Muon</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Dual-ascent step size</td>
<td id="A1.T5.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For Stiefel-managed weights, the manifold itself fixes singular values and provides implicit scale control. For DGram-managed weights, the diagonal of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W</annotation></semantics></math> is unconstrained, so no explicit scale control is applied in our experiments. This is a potential confound: weight decay or other scale regularization may stabilize DGram attention.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning-rate schedule.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both AdamW and Muon use the same cosine learning-rate schedule with linear warmup. The warmup period is 1,000 iterations, the cosine decay runs until 50,000 iterations, and the minimum AdamW learning rate is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>. The Muon learning rate is scaled proportionally to the AdamW schedule: if <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{AdamW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>AdamW</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{AdamW}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the AdamW learning rate at iteration <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, then the Muon learning rate is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{Muon}}=0.02\cdot\frac{\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{AdamW}}}{6\times 10^{-4}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>Muon</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>AdamW</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{Muon}}=0.02\cdot\frac{\eta_{t}^{\mathrm{AdamW}}}{6\times 10^{-4}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, AdamW and Muon share the same warmup and decay profile while retaining different peak learning rates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Manifold Muon implementation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement Manifold Muon as a tangent-space-constrained Muon update
followed by a retraction. For each Muon-managed matrix
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we internally transpose wide matrices
so that <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq n</annotation></semantics></math> before applying the operations below, and transpose
back at the end. Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Nesterov momentum direction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tangent constraint.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We characterize each manifold by a self-adjoint projector
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> acting on <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> symmetric matrices. The
tangent condition takes the unified form</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> selects the components of the symmetric Gram
differential that the manifold actually constrains. For Stiefel, the
constraint <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W=I</annotation></semantics></math> controls every entry of the Gram matrix, so
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{St}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>St</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{St}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the identity on symmetric matrices: the entire
symmetric part must vanish. For DGram, we constrain only the off-diagonal entries of the Gram
matrix. The projector is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathrm{DG}}(M)=M-\mathrm{Diag}(\mathrm{diag}(M))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>DG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{DG}}(M)=M-\mathrm{Diag}(\mathrm{diag}(M)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which selects the off-diagonal part of a symmetric matrix. The
resulting tangent condition</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Off}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Off}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">preserves <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Off}(W^{\top}W)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Off}(W^{\top}W)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the columns of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>
remain pairwise orthogonal. The diagonal entries of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W</annotation></semantics></math>,
which correspond to per-column scales (and hence to singular values
since the columns are orthogonal), are unconstrained. DGram is
therefore weaker than Stiefel: it preserves Gram diagonality but
does not force <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W=I</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The update direction <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by approximately solving</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{A\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}}\mathrm{tr}(G^{\top}A)\quad\mathrm{s.t.}\quad\|A\|_{2}\leq 1,\quad P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{A\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}}\mathrm{tr}(G^{\top}A)\quad\mathrm{s.t.}\quad\|A\|_{2}\leq 1,\quad P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the spectral norm. The corresponding
parameter step is then <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\mapsto W-\eta A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\mapsto W-\eta A</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> the Muon
learning rate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dual ascent.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We solve this problem by dual ascent over a multiplier
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the constraint depends
only on the symmetric part of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we pass
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}(\Lambda+\Lambda^{\top})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}(\Lambda+\Lambda^{\top})</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> in
the gradient computation; this also keeps the dual update
well-defined when <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> drifts away from symmetry during
iteration. The Lagrangian is linear in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> apart from the
spectral-norm bound, and its maximizer over the unit spectral-norm
ball is given by the matrix sign function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{\|A\|_{2}\leq 1}\mathrm{tr}(B^{\top}A)=\mathrm{msign}(B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>msign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{\|A\|_{2}\leq 1}\mathrm{tr}(B^{\top}A)=\mathrm{msign}(B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{msign}(B)=UV^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>msign</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{msign}(B)=UV^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for the compact SVD
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=U\Sigma V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=U\Sigma V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, equivalently the polar factor of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to the gradient of the Lagrangian, the inner-loop
update direction at multiplier <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}=\mathrm{msign}\!\left(G+2W\,P_{\mathcal{M}}\!\left(\tfrac{\Lambda_{k}+\Lambda_{k}^{\top}}{2}\right)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.634em;" width="2.634em"><mi>msign</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}=\mathrm{msign}\!\left(G+2W\,P_{\mathcal{M}}\!\left(\tfrac{\Lambda_{k}+\Lambda_{k}^{\top}}{2}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the factor <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> arises from the derivative of
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}A+A^{\top}W</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We initialize the multiplier with</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{0}=-\tfrac{1}{4}\,P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}G+G^{\top}W)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{0}=-\tfrac{1}{4}\,P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}G+G^{\top}W),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which we use as a simple linearized warm start for the dual ascent iterations. In practice, this reduces the number of inner iterations needed to obtain a small tangent-constraint violation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At inner iteration <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we measure the constraint violation</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}=P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A_{k}+A_{k}^{\top}W)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}=P_{\mathcal{M}}(W^{\top}A_{k}+A_{k}^{\top}W)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and update the multiplier as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{k+1}=\Lambda_{k}-\alpha\!\left(1-\tfrac{k}{K}\right)H_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.473em;" width="0.473em"><mi>α</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{k+1}=\Lambda_{k}-\alpha\!\left(1-\tfrac{k}{K}\right)H_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The factor <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-k/K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-k/K)</annotation></semantics></math> anneals the dual step size linearly to zero so
that the iterates settle within <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> inner steps rather than
oscillating around the constraint surface. We use <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=20</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> in all experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Retraction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After the inner loop, we form the trial update</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}=W-\eta A_{K}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}=W-\eta A_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and retract it back onto the assigned manifold. For Stiefel, the
retraction is the polar factor, computed via the matrix sign:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{St}}(\widetilde{W})=\mathrm{msign}(\widetilde{W})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>St</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>msign</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{St}}(\widetilde{W})=\mathrm{msign}(\widetilde{W}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For DGram, let the compact SVD of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}</annotation></semantics></math> be</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}=U\Sigma V^{\top},\qquad\Sigma=\mathrm{Diag}(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{n})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}=U\Sigma V^{\top},\qquad\Sigma=\mathrm{Diag}(\sigma_{1},\ldots,\sigma_{n}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We use the SVD-based retraction</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})=(UV^{\top})\,\Sigma." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>DG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})=(UV^{\top})\,\Sigma.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(UV^{\top})^{\top}(UV^{\top})=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(UV^{\top})^{\top}(UV^{\top})=I</annotation></semantics></math>, the retracted matrix satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})^{\top}R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})=\Sigma^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>DG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>DG</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})^{\top}R_{\mathrm{DG}}(\widetilde{W})=\Sigma^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which is diagonal but not in general the identity. The retraction
therefore eliminates off-diagonal Gram correlations while leaving
the diagonal entries (the squared singular values) free, giving
DGram its characteristic scale freedom relative to Stiefel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This ensures that each constrained weight starts on its assigned
manifold; subsequent updates are followed by the corresponding
retraction.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation and logging.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate training and validation loss every 1,000 iterations. Each evaluation loss is computed as the mean over 200 mini-batches sampled from the corresponding split. We also log per-iteration training loss, wall-clock time per step, learning rate, and model-flop utilization (MFU) estimates for monitoring. Evaluation metrics are saved as JSONL files for later plotting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Spectral diagnostics.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Muon-managed parameters in the manifold-constrained
configurations, we additionally save spectral statistics every
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. For each such weight matrix, we compute and
store its singular values, the Gram diagonal
<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{diag}(W^{\top}W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{diag}(W^{\top}W)</annotation></semantics></math>, the Frobenius norm of the
off-diagonal part of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W</annotation></semantics></math>, and the Frobenius norm <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.1 Singular Value Growth in Attention ‣ 4 Mechanistic Analysis: Why DGram Attention Fails" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we aggregate the spectral
logs by taking the maximum singular value over all matrices in each
parameter group at each logging step. The attention curve aggregates
over <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">attn.c_attn</span> and <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">attn.c_proj</span> across all
layers, while the MLP/FFN curve aggregates over <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mlp.c_fc</span>
and <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px10.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">mlp.c_proj</span>. We report the maximum rather than the mean
because the softmax-saturation mechanism depends on worst-case
spectral growth.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px11" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Instability criterion.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We classify a run as unstable if any of the following objective conditions are met during the 50,000-iteration schedule:</p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:2em;">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hard loss spike.</span> After iteration <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>, the
validation loss exceeds <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(2\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}},5.0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>loss</mi><mi>best</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(2\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}},5.0)</annotation></semantics></math> at any evaluation step.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Persistent drift.</span> The mean validation loss over the
final <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> of evaluations exceeds
<math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.2\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>loss</mi><mi>best</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.2\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the
run has departed from its best loss and not recovered.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Failure to recover from degradation.</span> After reaching
<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>loss</mi><mi>best</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the validation loss stays
above <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.05\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.05</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>loss</mi><mi>best</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.05\cdot\mathrm{loss}_{\mathrm{best}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the
remainder of training.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Early termination.</span> The run halts due to non-finite
loss before iteration <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>48,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48{,}000</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px11.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Configurations that meet any of these criteria are reported as unstable in Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 2.2 Layer-wise Manifold Assignments ‣ 2 Background and Setup" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Small fluctuations within
the stable trajectory of converged runs are not treated as
unstable.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Manifold Assignment Schematic</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The five manifold configurations are defined by which constraint
(Stiefel, DGram, or none) is applied to the attention and MLP/FFN
parameter groups; the parameter grouping is given in
Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Optimizer setup. ‣ Appendix A Experimental Details" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> of Appendix A, and the resulting
configurations and their final validation losses are summarized in
Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 2.2 Layer-wise Manifold Assignments ‣ 2 Background and Setup" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> of the main body. All non-Muon
parameters use AdamW with the same hyperparameters in every
configuration.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The HETERO configuration is the main heterogeneous assignment, with
Stiefel applied to attention and DGram applied to MLP/FFN. HETERO-INV
swaps these assignments and serves as a control: it tests whether
the benefit comes from the specific Stiefel-attention/DGram-MLP
pairing rather than from heterogeneity per se.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix B Manifold Assignment Schematic" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates the HETERO assignment
in the full GPT-2 architecture. Each of the 12 Transformer blocks
applies Stiefel Manifold Muon to its attention projections and DGram
Manifold Muon to its feed-forward projections, while all parameters
outside these blocks (input embedding, positional encoding, final
linear layer, layer-norm scales) are optimized with AdamW.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.13276v1/architecture-muon.png" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:337/476;" width="337" height="476" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>
Schematic of the HETERO manifold assignment in GPT-2. Within each
of the 12 Transformer blocks, attention projections are updated by
Stiefel Manifold Muon (orange) and MLP/FFN projections by DGram
Manifold Muon (blue). All remaining parameters—input embedding,
positional encoding, final linear layer, and normalization
scales—are optimized with AdamW (gray).
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof Sketches</h2>

<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Spectral consequences of Stiefel and DGram constraints.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq n</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}(W)\geq\cdots\geq\sigma_{n}(W)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}(W)\geq\cdots\geq\sigma_{n}(W)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> denote its singular
values. Under the Stiefel constraint,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W=I_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W=I_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for every <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Wv\|_{2}^{2}=v^{\top}W^{\top}Wv=\|v\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Wv\|_{2}^{2}=v^{\top}W^{\top}Wv=\|v\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence all singular values are equal to one:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(W)=1\qquad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(W)=1\qquad\text{for all }i=1,\ldots,n,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and in particular</p>
<table id="A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W\|_{2}=\sigma_{1}(W)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W\|_{2}=\sigma_{1}(W)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Thus Stiefel-constrained weights are spectrally bounded by construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">DGram imposes a weaker Gram constraint. In our implementation, DGram
constrains the off-diagonal entries of the Gram matrix,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Off}(W^{\top}W)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Off}(W^{\top}W)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W^{\top}W=D" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W^{\top}W=D</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for some diagonal matrix <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Writing</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\operatorname{Diag}(d_{1},\ldots,d_{n})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\operatorname{Diag}(d_{1},\ldots,d_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">we have, for every <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Wv\|_{2}^{2}=v^{\top}Dv=\sum_{j=1}^{n}d_{j}v_{j}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Wv\|_{2}^{2}=v^{\top}Dv=\sum_{j=1}^{n}d_{j}v_{j}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore the singular values of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{j}(W)=\sqrt{d_{j}},\qquad j=1,\ldots,n." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msqrt><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}(W)=\sqrt{d_{j}},\qquad j=1,\ldots,n.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Unlike Stiefel, DGram does not require <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W\|_{2}=\max_{j}\sqrt{d_{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W\|_{2}=\max_{j}\sqrt{d_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">is unconstrained by the manifold definition. In particular, for any
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the matrix</p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{c}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{n}\\
0\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{c}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{n}\\
0\end{bmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Off}(W_{c}^{\top}W_{c})=0,\qquad W_{c}^{\top}W_{c}=c^{2}I_{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Off}(W_{c}^{\top}W_{c})=0,\qquad W_{c}^{\top}W_{c}=c^{2}I_{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.9" class="ltx_p">but</p>
<table id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{c}\|_{2}=c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{c}\|_{2}=c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Thus DGram preserves Gram diagonality while permitting arbitrary
singular-value growth.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Attention logit amplification.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a single attention head with token representation matrix
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, query projection
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>, and key
projection <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The pre-softmax attention logit matrix is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\frac{XW_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\frac{XW_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By submultiplicativity of the spectral norm,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}=\left\|\frac{XW_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}^{\top}\|_{2}\|X^{\top}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}=\left\|\frac{XW_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}\right\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}^{\top}\|_{2}\|X^{\top}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{K}^{\top}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2},\qquad\|X^{\top}\|_{2}=\|X\|_{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{K}^{\top}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2},\qquad\|X^{\top}\|_{2}=\|X\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Thus the scale of the attention logits can grow multiplicatively with
the spectral norms of the query and key projections.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under Stiefel constraints on both <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Thus Stiefel attention rules out weight-induced amplification of the
attention logits.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Under DGram constraints, however, write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=D_{Q},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=D_{K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=D_{Q},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=D_{K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{Q},D_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{Q},D_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are diagonal but not necessarily identity. Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})},\qquad\|W_{K}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})},\qquad\|W_{K}\|_{2}=\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Consequently,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})}\sqrt{\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(D_{Q})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(D_{K})</annotation></semantics></math> are not fixed
by the DGram constraint, DGram attention permits weight-induced logit
amplification.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The same conclusion can be seen at the level of individual logits. For
tokens <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i},x_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i},x_{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}=\frac{x_{i}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}=\frac{x_{i}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">By Cauchy–Schwarz,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{ij}|\leq\frac{\|x_{i}\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}\|x_{j}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{ij}|\leq\frac{\|x_{i}\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}\|x_{j}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, even when token features are bounded, large singular values in
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> can enlarge the range of the attention logits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Softmax saturation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be a row of the attention logit matrix and
let</p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\operatorname{softmax}(z),\qquad p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{T}e^{z_{\ell}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\operatorname{softmax}(z),\qquad p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{T}e^{z_{\ell}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Assume without loss of generality that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}=\max_{i}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}=\max_{i}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define
the logit gap</p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=z_{1}-\max_{j\neq 1}z_{j}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=z_{1}-\max_{j\neq 1}z_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p_{1}=\frac{\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}{e^{z_{1}}+\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}\leq\frac{\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}{e^{z_{1}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p_{1}=\frac{\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}{e^{z_{1}}+\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}\leq\frac{\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}}{e^{z_{1}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}\leq z_{1}-\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}\leq z_{1}-\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}\leq(T-1)e^{z_{1}-\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\neq 1}e^{z_{j}}\leq(T-1)e^{z_{1}-\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-p_{1}\leq(T-1)e^{-\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-p_{1}\leq(T-1)e^{-\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Equivalently,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}\geq 1-(T-1)e^{-\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}\geq 1-(T-1)e^{-\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Thus, as the logit gap <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> grows, the softmax output approaches a
one-hot vector exponentially fast.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The Jacobian of the softmax is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)=\frac{\partial p}{\partial z}=\operatorname{Diag}(p)-pp^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)=\frac{\partial p}{\partial z}=\operatorname{Diag}(p)-pp^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\top}J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)u=\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}u_{i}^{2}-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}u_{i}\right)^{2}=\operatorname{Var}_{i\sim p}(u_{i})\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\top}J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)u=\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}u_{i}^{2}-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}u_{i}\right)^{2}=\operatorname{Var}_{i\sim p}(u_{i})\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">so <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite. Moreover,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)_{ii}=p_{i}(1-p_{i}),\qquad J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)_{ij}=-p_{i}p_{j}\quad(i\neq j)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)_{ii}=p_{i}(1-p_{i}),\qquad J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)_{ij}=-p_{i}p_{j}\quad(i\neq j).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is close to one, write</p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=1-p_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=1-p_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}=\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}=\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">The Frobenius norm satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}^{2}(1-p_{i})^{2}+\sum_{i\neq j}p_{i}^{2}p_{j}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{T}p_{i}^{2}(1-p_{i})^{2}+\sum_{i\neq j}p_{i}^{2}p_{j}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.7" class="ltx_p">The first diagonal term is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{2}(1-p_{1})^{2}\leq\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{2}(1-p_{1})^{2}\leq\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.8" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{2}(1-p_{j})^{2}\leq p_{j}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{2}(1-p_{j})^{2}\leq p_{j}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.9" class="ltx_p">and hence</p>
<table id="A3.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}(1-p_{j})^{2}\leq\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}\leq\left(\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}\right)^{2}=\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}(1-p_{j})^{2}\leq\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}\leq\left(\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}\right)^{2}=\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.10" class="ltx_p">For the off-diagonal terms,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\neq j}p_{i}^{2}p_{j}^{2}=\left(\sum_{i}p_{i}^{2}\right)^{2}-\sum_{i}p_{i}^{4}\leq 2p_{1}^{2}\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}+\left(\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}\right)^{2}\leq 2\varepsilon^{2}+\varepsilon^{4}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\neq j}p_{i}^{2}p_{j}^{2}=\left(\sum_{i}p_{i}^{2}\right)^{2}-\sum_{i}p_{i}^{4}\leq 2p_{1}^{2}\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}+\left(\sum_{j\neq 1}p_{j}^{2}\right)^{2}\leq 2\varepsilon^{2}+\varepsilon^{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.11" class="ltx_p">Combining these bounds gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}\leq 4\varepsilon^{2}+\varepsilon^{4}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}\leq 4\varepsilon^{2}+\varepsilon^{4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.12" class="ltx_p">and therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2\varepsilon+\varepsilon^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.13" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=1-p_{1}\leq(T-1)e^{-\Delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=1-p_{1}\leq(T-1)e^{-\Delta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A3.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)e^{-\Delta}+(T-1)^{2}e^{-2\Delta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)e^{-\Delta}+(T-1)^{2}e^{-2\Delta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.14" class="ltx_p">Thus large logit gaps make the softmax Jacobian exponentially small.
This formalizes the saturation mechanism: if spectral growth in
attention projections increases logit gaps, the softmax can enter a
nearly one-hot regime in which gradients through the attention
probabilities become small.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (DGram attention admits gradient-degenerate directions under bounded inputs). ‣ Gradient non-degeneracy. ‣ 4.2 Softmax Saturation and Gradient Degeneracy ‣ 4 Mechanistic Analysis: Why DGram Attention Fails" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now combine the preceding observations to show that DGram attention
can realize arbitrarily saturated softmax maps even when the input
features are bounded. This is not a statement about all DGram weights,
but rather an existence result showing that the DGram constraint alone
does not prevent gradient-degenerate attention.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and assume <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq d</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider DGram-feasible
query and key matrices of the form</p>
<table id="A3.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{d}\\
0\end{bmatrix},\qquad W_{K}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{d}\\
0\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{d}\\
0\end{bmatrix},\qquad W_{K}=c\begin{bmatrix}I_{d}\\
0\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">for some scale <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=c^{2}I_{d},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=c^{2}I_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=c^{2}I_{d},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=c^{2}I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">so</p>
<table id="A3.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Off}(W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q})=0,\qquad\operatorname{Off}(W_{K}^{\top}W_{K})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Off</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Off}(W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q})=0,\qquad\operatorname{Off}(W_{K}^{\top}W_{K})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are feasible under the DGram constraint, while</p>
<table id="A3.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now choose bounded token features <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\ldots,x_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\ldots,x_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> such that their first
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> coordinates contain distinguishable components. For example, take</p>
<table id="A3.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=\begin{bmatrix}e_{1}\\
0\end{bmatrix},\qquad x_{j}=\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\quad\text{for }j\neq 1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=\begin{bmatrix}e_{1}\\
0\end{bmatrix},\qquad x_{j}=\begin{bmatrix}0\\
0\end{bmatrix}\quad\text{for }j\neq 1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. These inputs satisfy</p>
<table id="A3.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq 1\qquad\text{for all }i." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq 1\qquad\text{for all }i.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For the first query row, the logits are</p>
<table id="A3.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{j}=\frac{x_{1}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{j}=\frac{x_{1}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A3.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}=\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}},\qquad z_{j}=0\quad\text{for }j\neq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}=\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}},\qquad z_{j}=0\quad\text{for }j\neq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.5" class="ltx_p">The logit gap is therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.6" class="ltx_p">By the softmax saturation bound above,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)\exp\!\left(-\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)+(T-1)^{2}\exp\!\left(-\frac{2c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)\exp\!\left(-\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right)+(T-1)^{2}\exp\!\left(-\frac{2c^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Consequently, for every <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a sufficiently
large <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}&lt;\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}&lt;\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.8" class="ltx_p">Thus DGram-feasible attention projections can induce arbitrarily small
softmax Jacobians on bounded inputs. In this precise sense, DGram
attention can become gradient-degenerate.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">More generally, the construction does not rely on the specific basis
choice above. If DGram allows</p>
<table id="A3.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=D_{Q},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=D_{K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=D_{Q},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=D_{K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">with large diagonal entries, then query-key inner products can be scaled
by the corresponding singular directions. Since DGram does not fix the
diagonal of the Gram matrix, it does not rule out this amplification
mechanism.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Stiefel attention is gradient non-degenerate under bounded inputs). ‣ Gradient non-degeneracy. ‣ 4.2 Softmax Saturation and Gradient Degeneracy ‣ 4 Mechanistic Analysis: Why DGram Attention Fails" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, Stiefel constraints remove the scale degree of freedom in
the query and key projections. If</p>
<table id="A3.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=I_{d},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=I_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=I_{d},\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=I_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For any bounded token features satisfying</p>
<table id="A3.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq R\qquad\text{for all }i," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq R\qquad\text{for all }i,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.4" class="ltx_p">each individual attention logit satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{ij}|=\left|\frac{x_{i}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}\right|\leq\frac{\|x_{i}\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}\|x_{j}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\leq\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{ij}|=\left|\frac{x_{i}^{\top}W_{Q}W_{K}^{\top}x_{j}}{\sqrt{d}}\right|\leq\frac{\|x_{i}\|_{2}\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}\|x_{j}\|_{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\leq\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore all logits lie in the interval</p>
<table id="A3.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}\in\left[-\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}},\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}\in\left[-\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}},\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.6" class="ltx_p">For any row <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, its maximum possible logit gap is bounded by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(z)=\max_{i}z_{i}-\max_{j\neq i^{\star}}z_{j}\leq\max_{i}z_{i}-\min_{j}z_{j}\leq\frac{2R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>j</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(z)=\max_{i}z_{i}-\max_{j\neq i^{\star}}z_{j}\leq\max_{i}z_{i}-\min_{j}z_{j}\leq\frac{2R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Thus Stiefel attention prevents the weights themselves from producing
arbitrarily large attention-logit gaps when the input features are
bounded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, at the matrix level,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This does not imply that softmax saturation is impossible, since
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the data-dependent geometry of the token features can
still affect the logits. It does imply, however, that Stiefel removes
the specific failure mode in which the query and key projection matrices
grow in spectral norm and amplify the logits through</p>
<table id="A3.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This is the sense in which Stiefel attention controls weight-induced
logit amplification.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Combined with the Frobenius-norm bound derived earlier, the bounded
logit range under Stiefel implies a positive lower bound on
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}\|_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}\|_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, if every logit lies in
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-M,M]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-M,M]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=R^{2}/\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=R^{2}/\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, then for every <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{T}e^{z_{\ell}}}\geq\frac{e^{-M}}{Te^{M}}=\frac{e^{-2M}}{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{\ell=1}^{T}e^{z_{\ell}}}\geq\frac{e^{-M}}{Te^{M}}=\frac{e^{-2M}}{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By the same argument applied to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{i}z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{i}z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, every <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is
also bounded above by <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-(T-1)e^{-2M}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-(T-1)e^{-2M}/T</annotation></semantics></math>, so each <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> lies
in <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a_{T},1-a_{T}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a_{T},1-a_{T}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{T}=e^{-2M}/T&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{T}=e^{-2M}/T&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}\geq T\,a_{T}^{2}(1-a_{T})^{2}=:c(T,d,R)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z)\|_{F}^{2}\geq T\,a_{T}^{2}(1-a_{T})^{2}=:c(T,d,R)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.2" class="ltx_p">which is independent of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is the lower bound
asserted in Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Stiefel attention is gradient non-degenerate under bounded inputs). ‣ Gradient non-degeneracy. ‣ 4.2 Softmax Saturation and Gradient Degeneracy ‣ 4 Mechanistic Analysis: Why DGram Attention Fails" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scope of the argument.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The preceding derivation should be interpreted as a mechanistic
explanation rather than a complete proof of training instability. The
mathematical statement is that DGram does not impose a uniform spectral
bound on the query and key projections. Equivalently, DGram admits
feasible sequences
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{W_{Q}^{(c)},W_{K}^{(c)}\}_{c\to\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{W_{Q}^{(c)},W_{K}^{(c)}\}_{c\to\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Off}\!\left((W_{Q}^{(c)})^{\top}W_{Q}^{(c)}\right)=\operatorname{Off}\!\left((W_{K}^{(c)})^{\top}W_{K}^{(c)}\right)=0,\qquad\|W_{Q}^{(c)}\|_{2}\|W_{K}^{(c)}\|_{2}\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.815em;" width="1.815em"><mi>Off</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.815em;" width="1.815em"><mi>Off</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Off}\!\left((W_{Q}^{(c)})^{\top}W_{Q}^{(c)}\right)=\operatorname{Off}\!\left((W_{K}^{(c)})^{\top}W_{K}^{(c)}\right)=0,\qquad\|W_{Q}^{(c)}\|_{2}\|W_{K}^{(c)}\|_{2}\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For suitable bounded inputs, the corresponding attention logits</p>
<table id="A3.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{(c)}=\frac{XW_{Q}^{(c)}(W_{K}^{(c)})^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{(c)}=\frac{XW_{Q}^{(c)}(W_{K}^{(c)})^{\top}X^{\top}}{\sqrt{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">contain a row <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math> whose logit gap satisfies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{c}=\max_{i}z_{i}^{(c)}-\max_{j\neq i^{\star}}z_{j}^{(c)}\to\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{c}=\max_{i}z_{i}^{(c)}-\max_{j\neq i^{\star}}z_{j}^{(c)}\to\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i^{\star}=\arg\max_{i}z_{i}^{(c)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i^{\star}=\arg\max_{i}z_{i}^{(c)}</annotation></semantics></math>. The softmax Jacobian bound
then gives</p>
<table id="A3.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z^{(c)})\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)e^{-\Delta_{c}}+(T-1)^{2}e^{-2\Delta_{c}}\to 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>sm</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J_{\mathrm{sm}}(z^{(c)})\|_{F}\leq 2(T-1)e^{-\Delta_{c}}+(T-1)^{2}e^{-2\Delta_{c}}\to 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, DGram permits feasible attention weights along which the softmax
map becomes arbitrarily close to a one-hot routing map and its Jacobian
becomes arbitrarily small.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By contrast, Stiefel constraints remove this particular scale degree of
freedom. If</p>
<table id="A3.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=I,\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=I," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}^{\top}W_{Q}=I,\qquad W_{K}^{\top}W_{K}=I,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}=\|W_{K}\|_{2}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and hence the attention logits obey the uniform weight-induced bound</p>
<table id="A3.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|_{2}\leq\frac{\|X\|_{2}^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.4" class="ltx_p">For token features satisfying <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x_{i}\|_{2}\leq R</annotation></semantics></math>, this also implies the
entrywise bound</p>
<table id="A3.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{ij}|\leq\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{ij}|\leq\frac{R^{2}}{\sqrt{d}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore Stiefel attention rules out the specific mechanism in which
query and key weights grow in spectral norm and amplify attention logits
through the factor <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|W_{Q}\|_{2}\|W_{K}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This argument does not imply that every DGram-attention training run
must become unstable, nor does it imply that Stiefel attention guarantees
non-degenerate gradients for all inputs or all optimization
trajectories. In a full Transformer, the attention logits also depend on
LayerNorm, residual connections, multiple heads, value and output
projections, optimizer state, and the data distribution. These effects
can modify the simplified single-head picture analyzed above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The intended conclusion is therefore narrower: DGram allows a
weight-space direction along which attention logits can become
arbitrarily sharp, whereas Stiefel removes that weight-induced
amplification pathway. This contrast is consistent with our empirical
observation that configurations assigning DGram to attention exhibit
rapid singular-value growth and unstable training, while configurations
with Stiefel attention remain stable in our experiments.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section><div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:creator" content="\icmlfullauthorlist"></div>
<div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:subject" content="weight-space geometry, manifold optimization, Manifold Muon, training dynamics"></div>
<div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:subject" content="ICML 2026 Workshop on Weight-Space Symmetries"></div>
<div class="ltx_rdf" about="" property="dcterms:title" content="Different Layers, Different Manifolds: \\
Module-Wise Weight-Space Geometry in Transformer Optimization"></div>

</article>
</div>
</div>
